  "notes": "West leads the ♦8 against 4♥. East plays the ♦Q and South should win the ♦A in order to prevent the defense from scoring an immediate diamond ruff. South has a certain diamond loser so he must hold his trump losers to 2. South must play with care as East's opening bid marks him with the ♥A.\n\nSouth should cross to the dummy at trick 2 and start trump by leading dummy's ♥6. If East ducks, South can win the ♥Q and play a second round of trump to East's ♥A. South will still have to lose a heart trick and a diamond trick, but the contract will be secure.\n\nIf East chooses to rise with the ♥A on the first round of the suit, giving up his second natural trump trick, South will still survive. East is welcome to cash the ♦K and give West a diamond ruff, but there will be only 2 trumps outstanding and the ♥K and ♥Q can take care of these.",
  "commentary_paragraphs": [
    "West leads the ♦8 against 4♥. East plays the ♦Q and South should win the ♦A in order to prevent the defense from scoring an immediate diamond ruff. South has a certain diamond loser so he must hold his trump losers to 2. South must play with care as East's opening bid marks him with the ♥A.",
    "South should cross to the dummy at trick 2 and start trump by leading dummy's ♥6. If East ducks, South can win the ♥Q and play a second round of trump to East's ♥A. South will still have to lose a heart trick and a diamond trick, but the contract will be secure.",
    "If East chooses to rise with the ♥A on the first round of the suit, giving up his second natural trump trick, South will still survive. East is welcome to cash the ♦K and give West a diamond ruff, but there will be only 2 trumps outstanding and the ♥K and ♥Q can take care of these."
  ],
